    "body": "### What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #8021. for codecontests/apps/codeforces/taco the code scorer re-runs only the first 10 tests after a failure and scores passed/10, so a program right on 1-10 and wrong on 11 got 1.0. now a wrong answer the full run already saw past test 10 is counted (10/11). timeouts and runtime errors keep the current behaviour since the second pass is there to give slow tests more time (#1921). sandbox_fusion gets the same rule so both paths still match\n\n### Checklist Before Starting\n\n- [x] Search for similar PRs: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=prime_code+continuous , closest are #7254 and #7853 which touch process cleanup and the call based wrapper, not scoring\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}`\n\n### Test\n\nadded test_prime_code_wrong_answer_after_first_ten_cases (real execution) and test_unit_continuous_score_counts_wrong_answer_after_first_ten (mocked check_correctness). both fail on main with 1.0 != 0.909 and pass here\n\n    pytest tests/utils/reward_score tests/workers/reward_manager\n    28 passed, 13 skipped\n\nran on macos with the multiprocessing start method set to fork (the linux default), under spawn test_prime_code and test_prime_math already fail on main for pickling reasons. existing expectations (1.0, 0.9 for first 9 of 11 pass, prime_code == sandbox_fusion) are unchanged. didnt check how many real dataset problems hit this\n\n### API and Usage Example\n\nno API change\n\n### Design & Code Changes\n\nprime_code/__init__.py and sandbox_fusion/__init__.py, about 9 lines\n\n### Checklist Before Submitting\n\n- [x] Read the Contribute Guide\n- [x] Apply pre-commit checks\n- [ ] Add / Update the documentation, not needed\n- [x] Add unit or end-to-end test(s)\n\nused an AI assistant to help write the change and tests, reviewed it and ran the tests above\n",
