    {
      "body": "Reviewed at a5aef7cd. I independently exercised both scoring paths with the same boundary controls: ten passes followed by a known wrong answer now yields 10/11, while a timeout/error sentinel after the first ten preserves the existing 1.0 behavior. The two implementations remain aligned, and the focused regression coverage checks both real prime-code execution and the Sandbox Fusion calculation. I also checked the diff for whitespace errors and found no competing open or closed PR for this scoring boundary.",
